.TH tuini n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tuini
.PP
INI reader/writer. Parses into a dict section \-> (dict key \-> value); keys before any \fB[section]\fR live in the global section "". Order is preserved. Comments (\fB;\fR or \fB#\fR) are dropped. A key that occurs twice in a section keeps the last value (the Windows profile API takes the first). Blanks around keys and values are dropped, so a value cannot end in a blank.
.PP
\fBsetValue\fR, \fBaddSection\fR and \fBtoIni\fR refuse what INI cannot hold, so \fBtoIni\fR never writes text that \fBparse\fR cannot read back (0.2; 0.1 wrote it):
.IP \(bu
a value with a line break;
.IP \(bu
a key with \fB=\fR or a line break, a key starting with \fB;\fR, \fB#\fR or \fB[\fR, a key with blanks at either end;
.IP \(bu
a section name with \fB]\fR or a line break, or blanks at either end.
.PP
Error code \fB{TCLUTILS TUINI VALUE}\fR.
.CS
tuini::parse iniText            ;# -> data dict
tuini::toIni data               ;# -> INI text
tuini::sections data
tuini::keys data ?section?
tuini::get  data section key ?default?
tuini::has  data section key
tuini::setValue data section key value   ;# -> new data dict
.CE
.PP
Error codes: \fB{TCLUTILS TUINI SYNTAX}\fR (parse), \fB{TCLUTILS TUINI VALUE}\fR (see above).
.SS "Additional exported commands"
.PP
Documented for completeness (same module, also covered by the test suite):
.CS
tuini::addSection data section                 ;# return a copy of data with an (empty) section ensured to exist
tuini::removeKey data section key              ;# return a copy of data with a key removed from a section
tuini::removeSection data section              ;# return a copy of data with a whole section removed
.CE
